# Product documentation

`docs/product/` is the behavioral source of truth for Phase 1.

## Rules

- Prefer updating Phase 1 or the matching UX flow over inventing behavior in code docs.
- Preserve UX flow document-control tables, confidence summaries, and evidence gaps.
- Do not treat deferred Phase 1 features as shipped; coming-soon is allowed only when honest.
- Keep notes short; promote durable structure changes to ADRs under `docs/architecture/decisions/`.
- Admin UX flows are Persian-label aware; keep wording consistent with existing flows.

## Index

- `docs/product/README.md`
- Phase 1: `docs/product/phase-1-application-features.md`
- UX flows: `docs/product/ux-flows/`
- Notes: `docs/product/notes/`
- Doc standards: `docs/quality/documentation.md`
